WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.512 --> 00:00:13.394
Hank frowned at the sketch on his desk.

2
00:00:14.915 --> 00:00:19.799
His class was having a T-shirt contest for Earth Day, and each student had to create a logo.

3
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:22.241
Then Mrs.

4
00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:25.223
Getty would choose a winner and order T-shirts for everyone.

5
00:00:26.444 --> 00:00:30.468
Hank had sketched a green frog with a speech bubble that read Think Green.

6
00:00:31.512 --> 00:00:33.393
But he didn't like his design very much.

7
00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:38.857
He added a superhero cape and a new speech bubble: Fight for Earth.

8
00:00:38.877 --> 00:00:43.160
"That's better," he thought.

9
00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:49.224
"But—" Anna suddenly poked him with her pencil.

10
00:00:52.927 --> 00:00:54.448
logo," she whispered.

11
00:00:54.468 --> 00:00:58.691
"Thanks." Hank was still frowning.

12
00:00:58.711 --> 00:01:00.092
"I don't like it."

13
00:01:01.624 --> 00:01:01.984
"I do.

14
00:01:02.564 --> 00:01:05.665
I hate to draw and—" "Anna and Hank!"

15
00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:07.346
Mrs. Getty said sharply.

16
00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:11.967
"You're supposed to be writing book reviews—not talking."

17
00:01:11.987 --> 00:01:15.468
"Sorry," Hank mumbled.

18
00:01:15.488 --> 00:01:20.090
"It's time for math now," the teacher said to the class.

19
00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:24.191
"You can finish your reviews later—for homework."

20
00:01:25.291 --> 00:01:26.211
Everyone groaned.

21
00:01:29.524 --> 00:01:34.427
As Hank flipped his notebook closed, a burst of air sent papers flying off his desk.

22
00:01:35.408 --> 00:01:36.828
Sighing, he scooped them up.

23
00:01:37.489 --> 00:01:41.611
"Ugh," he thought.

24
00:01:42.091 --> 00:01:44.293
He hadn't even finished reading his book yet.

25
00:01:45.333 --> 00:01:48.175
Writing this dumb book review would take forever.

26
00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:55.699
Hank started his homework right after dinner, but as he read, his thoughts kept drifting to the T-shirt

27
00:01:55.759 --> 00:02:00.001
contest. "I'll just draw for a few minutes," he thought.

28
00:02:00.021 --> 00:02:02.441
"Then I'll finish reading."

29
00:02:04.222 --> 00:02:05.882
Hank quickly sketched some ideas.

30
00:02:08.203 --> 00:02:12.204
Next he used colored pencils to add color and details to several designs.

31
00:02:14.985 --> 00:02:17.866
He didn't notice the time until his phone suddenly beeped.

32
00:02:17.886 --> 00:02:21.267
"Ack!" he cried.

33
00:02:21.287 --> 00:02:23.328
"My book review!

34
00:02:23.648 --> 00:02:24.628
I lost track of time!"

35
00:02:26.124 --> 00:02:27.465
Hank reached for his phone.

36
00:02:29.686 --> 00:02:33.387
Before he could stop himself, he searched the internet for the title of his book.

37
00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:39.870
A link popped up, which took him to a website with hundreds of book reviews.

38
00:02:42.611 --> 00:02:44.332
"Perfect," he whispered.

39
00:02:45.553 --> 00:02:51.495
He began copying a review into his notebook, and fifteen minutes later his homework was done.

40
00:02:53.488 --> 00:02:54.848
On Friday afternoon Mrs.

41
00:02:54.888 --> 00:02:56.349
Getty stood at the front of the room.

42
00:02:56.369 --> 00:03:00.730
"It's time to announce our contest winner."

43
00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:04.691
"Yes!" Hank pumped his fist.

44
00:03:04.711 --> 00:03:07.912
"All the designs are wonderful."

45
00:03:08.312 --> 00:03:09.953
She flashed a smile at Hank.

46
00:03:09.973 --> 00:03:14.074
"Some are very elaborate.

47
00:03:15.014 --> 00:03:17.735
But I chose one that will work well on a T-shirt.

48
00:03:19.095 --> 00:03:21.676
The winner is Anna!"

49
00:03:23.885 --> 00:03:26.387
"Anna?" Hank gasped as Mrs.

50
00:03:26.447 --> 00:03:28.088
Getty held up Anna's design.

51
00:03:28.108 --> 00:03:32.272
"Huh?" Hank blinked.

52
00:03:34.654 --> 00:03:37.496
Anna's logo was a frog in a superhero cape!

53
00:03:38.857 --> 00:03:41.559
At recess Hank stalked over to Anna.

54
00:03:41.579 --> 00:03:44.722
"You stole my design!"

55
00:03:46.203 --> 00:03:47.444
Anna's face turned red.

56
00:03:47.464 --> 00:03:49.826
"I'm sorry, Hank!

57
00:03:50.187 --> 00:03:53.133
Your sketch fell on the floor, and you said you didn't like it.

58
00:03:53.413 --> 00:03:56.134
So—" "So you stole it!"

59
00:03:56.715 --> 00:03:57.395
Hank snapped.

60
00:03:59.336 --> 00:04:01.838
"Don't you know it's wrong to steal other people's ideas?

61
00:04:02.218 --> 00:04:03.739
It's called plagiarism!"

62
00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:06.921
Anna bit her lip.

63
00:04:07.881 --> 00:04:08.641
"I'll tell Mrs.

64
00:04:08.702 --> 00:04:09.902
Getty after recess."

65
00:04:09.922 --> 00:04:16.946
"Good!" When they got back to the classroom, Anna started slowly toward the teacher.

66
00:04:19.147 --> 00:04:20.008
Hank watched her.

67
00:04:23.604 --> 00:04:24.344
"I'm glad Mrs.

68
00:04:24.404 --> 00:04:27.746
Getty will find out that I designed that logo," he thought.

69
00:04:29.947 --> 00:04:34.149
Just then his eyes landed on his notebook, and he felt a jolt.

70
00:04:34.169 --> 00:04:38.591
"I stole someone's ideas too," he realized.

71
00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:42.492
"I plagiarized my book review."

72
00:04:44.613 --> 00:04:46.514
Hank stood up, grabbing his notebook.

73
00:04:48.135 --> 00:04:49.395
He needed to talk to Mrs.

74
00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:49.976
Getty too.
